  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Morocco Earthquake Response 2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Around 11pm local time on September 8, a 6.8 magnitude earthquake struck the High Atlas mountain range, 72 km southwest of Marrakech, Morocco, a city home to 840,000 people. The quake was followed by a 4.9 magnitude aftershock. This has been the biggest earthquake felt in the region. Extensive damage has been reported with buildings collapsed and critical infrastructure severely damaged. GlobalMedic&apos;s Rapid Response Team is on the ground providing support to those affected by the quake.</narrative>
  </description>
